Title: A change of tactic is not a beat
Structure: sequence

# The Divorce

[[id: q1]]

[[goal: divorce | id: divorce | subject: WIFE | object: HUSBAND]]

[[goal: protect | id: reputation | subject: HUSBAND | object: his reputation]]

INT. HOUSE - BEDROOM - DAY

[[beat: He drowns her out | ahead: HUSBAND]]

The WIFE lets herself in with her key. The HUSBAND, on the bed, shuts his eyes and starts to sing.

HUSBAND
(singing, loud)
La la la la la!

WIFE
I want --

He sings louder.

WIFE
(shouting)
I want a --

Louder still. He puts his fingers in his ears.

[[beat: She writes it where he must read it | ahead: WIFE]]

She stops. Takes a lipstick from the dresser and writes one word across his shaving mirror, then turns it to face him.

He opens one eye. Reads it. The singing dies in his throat.
